 "sources": {
  "daypart_dimineata_ro": [
   "Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale ro",
   "(https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),",
   "transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as [05:00, 12:00).",
   "Sources: dexonline, Dictionarul explicativ al limbii romane",
   "(https://dexonline.ro/definitie/dupa-amiaza).",
   "Romanian opens the morning at 05:00. The articulated form dimineata is",
   "the everyday one (\"maine dimineata\") and is listed beside the bare noun."
  ],
  "daypart_dupa_amiaza_ro": [
   "Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale ro",
   "(https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),",
   "transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as [12:00, 18:00).",
   "The hyphenated surface is tokenizer-canonicalised to \"dupa amiaza\" (the",
   "hyphen splits into two tokens the loader re-glues) -- the same reason",
   "fr's daypart_apres_midi_fr.voc keeps this comment. Registering it here is",
   "required because bare \"amiaza\" is ALSO this locale's word for noon",
   "(clock_landmark_720.voc): without the glued multi-token surface, the",
   "hyphen-split \"amiaza\" half of \"dupa-amiaza\" was claimed by the noon",
   "landmark instead of the afternoon band."
  ],
  "daypart_noapte_ro": [
   "Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale ro",
   "(https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),",
   "transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as [22:00, 05:00).",
   "Sources: dexonline, Dictionarul explicativ al limbii romane",
   "(https://dexonline.ro/definitie/dupa-amiaza).",
   "The chart lists noapte twice, at 00:00 and again at 22:00: one band",
   "split only by the start-time notation, joined here into the single",
   "midnight-crossing night it is. Romanian is the only language of the",
   "thirteen where that join fires."
  ],
  "daypart_seara_ro": [
   "Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale ro",
   "(https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),",
   "transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as [18:00, 22:00).",
   "Sources: dexonline, Dictionarul explicativ al limbii romane",
   "(https://dexonline.ro/definitie/dupa-amiaza)."
  ],
  "marker_date_lead": [
   "Words that open a date or a clock time and belong to it.",
   "Each word is shown opening a time or date phrase on the page named in brackets,",
   "saved under knowledge/wiki/audits/chronologia/parity-fixes/marker-strand/sources/ in the workspace.",
   "pe: Wiktionary \"pe\": \"on (some time during the day of): pe zece mai\" [ro-pe.wikitext.txt]"
  ],
  "month_1": [
   "Unicode CLDR 47, locale ro, gregorian calendar (cldr-json",
   "cldr-dates-full/main/ro/ca-gregorian.json): months.format.wide,",
   "months.stand-alone.wide, months.format.abbreviated,",
   "months.stand-alone.abbreviated.  CLDR spells the abbreviations with a",
   "trailing period; the surfaces here drop it."
  ],
  "month_10": [
   "Unicode CLDR 47, locale ro, gregorian calendar (cldr-json",
   "cldr-dates-full/main/ro/ca-gregorian.json): months.format.wide,",
   "months.stand-alone.wide, months.format.abbreviated,",
   "months.stand-alone.abbreviated.  CLDR spells the abbreviations with a",
   "trailing period; the surfaces here drop it."
